From cb3dd70fd17eb2c6563f6e62b7bb7cc13c9dfa2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:06:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(auth): disables match per record by id, label,
 workspace account or secret fingerprint

Review of 8030b3ee106:
- token_disabled missed env/borrowed Anthropic rows (their persisted copy keeps only
  secret_fingerprint), so ANTHROPIC_TOKEN of a disabled row was served again. Records now carry a
  non-reversible 'fp' and tokens are compared by fingerprint too.
- the Codex resolver's pool-only fallback (_pool_codex_credential) handed out a disabled row's
  token to plugin requests / usage / aux; it now skips disabled rows (not for read-only status).
- account_of uses the ChatGPT workspace id before the email, so a personal and a Team workspace
  of one email are separate accounts.
- matching is per record: a record naming an account never hits a row whose token names another
  (also for label hits), and a re-seeded borrowed row with a new id stays disabled by fingerprint.

Proof: 6 tests RED with the fixes reverted, GREEN with them (49 in the feature files); 249 files
of pool/auth/codex/xai/delegate/routing/model-switch tests: 2486 passed.
